      "id": 1,
      "text": "Voluntown was named for colonial volunteers in 1675 King Philip's War who stayed to fight and did not leave.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Voluntown%2C_Connecticut"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Incorporated in 1721, Voluntown grew around textile mills, a Civilian Conservation Corps camp, and preserved historic buildings.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Voluntown%2C_Connecticut"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Village Center houses the Town Hall, Library, K‑8 school, Constitution Field, a walking track, and a gazebo.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://ctvisit.com/listings/town-voluntown"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Two-thirds of Voluntown’s 39.8‑square‑mile area is covered by state forest, including Pachaug State Forest.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
